> I'm trying to convert several types of unformatted files from
> Cray machines (C90 and T3E) to ES40 machines.
> Unformatted DIRECT-access files work well with "-convert big_endian" F90 
> parameter or something equivalent with OPEN statement.
> Unformatted SEQUENTIAL-access files seem to be more difficult.
> Does anyone have a solution to this problem or some reference on the net ?

You're talking about FORTRAN data files, right ?
If I remember correctly sequential files are organized in records,
with the record length as a binary 4-byte number attached before and
after the data portion. This way the FORTRAN runtime can walk forth and back
through data files consisting of data records with variable length. 



