Gavin wrote:
> 
> can someone tell me where I can download UNIX Os???
> thanks for your help

Depends on what platform you are talking about and what exactly you
want...

If you want a free UNIX-style operating system for almost any x86,
Alpha, VAX, HP, SGI, Sun, etc box... Check out Linux
(http://www.linux.org) and/or NetBSD (http://www.netbsd.org). If you are
strictly x86, then you might also want to see OpenBSD
(http://www.openbsd.org) and/or FreeBSD (http://www.freebsd.org). See a
pattern yet?

If you are wanting commercial UNIXes, then you will probably need to
PURCHASE them from the respective companies. Solaris from Sun, Tru64
UNIX from Compaq, and so on... If you are of the "personal use" or
"educational use" persuasion, Sun and Compaq both have special deals.

-- 

Until soon...
