I am porting some code from OpenVMS (Alpha) to TRU64, but have come
upon a few problems, quite serious from my perspective, with the compiler,
or rather lack of comformity (it seems).

Under OpenVMS i make regular use of the following pragmas, defined
<builtins.h>
and supported within PALCODE.


_PROBER + _PROBEW
""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""
allows you to probe a buffer for read and/or write access. Most useful when
writing API's,  typical usage is to ensure that the underlying API has r/w
access
to the callers buffer.

_INSQTI + INSQHI
""""""""""""""""""""""""""
This function inserts an entry at the front of a longword queue in an
indivisible
manner. This operation is interlocked against similar operations by other
processors
or devices in the system. Useful for enqueing work items from within an
AST (signal handler), when the non-ast code be be SIMULATANEOUSLY
de-queueing a work item, i.e you dont need to disable AST's/Block Signals.
Also useful when using Pthreads.

Examining the TRU64 documentation, there seems to be no equivalent.

Q1) Do these functions exist, or an equivalent, if so where, and what are
they called

Q2) Assuming these functions don't exist, can anyone (from ComPaq) comment
        as to why they are not present, bearing in mind they are PALCODE
        routines.


TIA









