If you know what is stored on each tape volume, you can load that tape
volume first.  Otherwise, I recommend you load the last volume (tape 3)
first.  Each tape header contains a block that identifies the tape set and
the contents of the previous volume in a multi-volume tape set.  Vrestore
doesn't have the intelligence to tell you which tape to mount, but it does
have enough intelligence to determine that the files you are searching for
are not on the tape in a very short space of time.

