Yao-Lu Tsai wrote:

> Dear all,
>
> I need to implement a critical section on TRU64 UNIX.
> Is there any function or system call like test_and_set
> or compare_and_swap on TRU64 UNIX ?

There's an undocumented routine in the C RTL called
msem_tas() or some such. Do an nm on the library
and grep for 'tas'.

Also, if you're using threads, consider using a mutex.

If you're not using threads, you can do what you want with
the load-locked/store-conditional instructions. Grap
around in /usr/include and look for asm directives
you can clone.




