Dave Lugo wrote:

> Here are the error messages, any assistance appreciated :)
>
> Thanks,
>
> Dave
>
> Here is a snippet:
>
> ld_mmap: Could not malloc 206160. bytes, for
> libD/OSF_4_0_ALPHA/libAgUiP.a(AgUiSnHfPwrI.o),  didnt attempt to mmap
> ld_mmap: Could not malloc 206160. bytes, for
> libD/OSF_4_0_ALPHA/libAgUiP.a(AgUiSnHfPwrI.o),  didnt attempt to mmap
> file                                 file_offset / flen -- pg bndry file
> offst --> last file offst mmapd
> mmap usage info not available; max of 160. slots
> Fatal error in: /usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/ld IOT/Abort trap
> ...failed Link binDS/OSF_4_0_ALPHA/PlFireSatVO ...

In addition to your guesses about swap or process limits, it could also
indicate
a known linker problem.   In some early versions of V4.0x the linker would
die like this when doing 'cxx' links.  (The cxx command runs the linker
in a special 'find unresolved symbols only mode' to help it figure out how
to do template instantiation - there was a bug in that special mode that
would cause failures like you see).  Fixed in the all the relevant patch
kits - install the latests patches.

Craig




